    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=mWm6e": {
      "title": "School Manager",
      "description": "School Manager - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies School Manager School Manager Provide strategic and operational leadership within the School, partnering closely with the Head of School and School Leadership Team Lead financial, people and resource management, ensuring effective planning, compliance and delivery across the School Drive operational improvement and strategic projects, including process improvement and digital transformation Permanent, full-time role based at AUT's Akoranga or City Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works, AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. About the Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences AUT’s Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences is a vibrant, interdisciplinary academic community committed to improving health, wellbeing and environmental sustainability locally and globally. The Faculty brings together leading educators, researchers and practitioners across health sciences, public health, rehabilitation, sport and exercise science, food science, chemistry, biology, biomedical science, and environmental science, with a strong emphasis on applied learning and real-world impact. Staff benefit from close links with industry, iwi, communities and government, opportunities for collaborative and translational research, and a culture that values innovation, equity and social responsibility. The Faculty offers an engaging, supportive environment for talented academics who want their teaching and research to make a meaningful difference in Aotearoa New Zealand and beyond. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi This is a senior leadership opportunity to provide strategic and operational oversight across two Schools within AUT's Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences. Reporting to the Director – Faculty Operations and working closely with the Head of School and School Leadership Team, you will provide leadership across the School's financial, administrative, people and operational functions. You will be a key point of contact for operational matters, providing advice and support that enables the School to achieve its strategic and academic objectives. You will lead operational planning, budget management, workforce and HR processes, facilities and resource management, and ensure effective systems and processes are in place to support the School's activities. You'll also contribute to faculty-wide priorities and initiatives through special projects and portfolio responsibilities. A key part of the role will be identifying opportunities to improve how the School operates, including process improvement and responsible use of digital tools and technology. You'll work collaboratively across the School, Faculty and wider University with stakeholders including People and Culture, Finance and Procurement, Estates and ICT. This role requires sound judgement, strong relationship management and the ability to work confidently across a complex tertiary environment. You'll bring a practical, solutions-focused approach while balancing strategic priorities with the day-to-day operational needs of the School. You will also play an important leadership role in embedding AUT's Te Aronui framework, values and commitment to creating equitable and mana-enhancing outcomes. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff. About you | Ko wai koe As an experienced operations leader, you'll bring the ability to balance strategic thinking with strong operational delivery. You'll be comfortable working across a broad portfolio of financial, people, administrative and organisational responsibilities and able to build trusted relationships across a complex organisation. You'll have strong judgement, initiative and problem-solving skills, with the ability to influence and work collaboratively with a wide range of stakeholders. Experience working within a tertiary environment would be highly valued. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi, Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting equity, diversity and inclusion initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: Relevant tertiary qualification and significant experience in operations management within a medium to large organisation Experience in financial management, budgeting and resource planning, with a sound understanding of accounting principles and processes Strong people leadership, organisational and administrative skills, with experience managing complex HR processes Excellent communication, relationship management and influencing skills, with the ability to work effectively across a diverse stakeholder group Experience leading projects, change initiatives and process improvements High digital fluency, including experience with financial management systems and Microsoft 365 applications Strategic thinking and strong problem-solving skills, combined with a practical and solutions-focused approach A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey. How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: To be agreed with the successful candidate. Salary Range | Ngā Utu: $110,000 - $131,000 commensurate with the skills and experience of the successful candidate. For further information: Contact Caroline Cranston, AUT Recruitment Consultant – caroline.cranston@aut.ac.nz Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 18th October 2026 at 5pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96459 Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week. At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96459 Location (s) North Campus, City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 18 Oct 2026 17:00 Expertise Administration Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 11053 - School Manager.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 29 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
