    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=EYs9e": {
      "title": "Technology Experience & Enablement Senior Manager",
      "description": "Technology Experience & Enablement Senior Manager - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Technology Experience & Enablement Senior Manager Technology Experience & Enablement Senior Manager Lead AUT’s digital workplace strategy and technology experience. Drive innovation through AI, automation and modern workplace technologies. Permanent, full-time role based at AUT's City Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT’s award-winning ICT Services are at the heart of the university’s digital future, delivering secure, reliable, and innovative technology services that support worldclass teaching, research, and student experiences. Spanning enterprise systems, digital platforms, infrastructure, data and analytics, artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, and customer focused support, the directorate works in close partnership with academic and professional teams to drive meaningful change. With close to 150 staff, ICT Services are committed to contributing to AUT's undertaking of preparing future-ready graduates. They are responsible for the technology that supports educators, researchers and students, in New Zealand's only University of Technology. They offer talented technologists the opportunity to work at scale, and contribute to a values-led organisation that invests in its people, embraces innovation, and is shaping a more connected, future-focused AUT. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi The Technology Experience & Enablement Senior Manager is a permanent full time role, that leads AUT's digital workplace strategy and the team responsible for delivering exceptional technology experiences to students, researchers, and staff. The role ensures AUT's technology ecosystem is secure, intelligent, accessible, and continuously evolving to support productivity, collaboration, engagement, and innovation across the University. You will be responsible for driving the adoption of modern workplace technologies, artificial intelligence, automation, and digital experience initiatives that enable AUT's strategic ambitions. Reporting to the Director Client Facing Technology, the Technology Experience & Enablement Senior Manager provides strategic and operational leadership across AUT's modern workplace and digital experience portfolio. This includes endpoint management (Microsoft and Apple), Microsoft 365 services, collaboration platforms, identity services, employee experience technologies, digital adoption, and AI-enabled productivity solutions. The role balances long-term strategy with delivery excellence, leading multidisciplinary teams that ensure technology delivers meaningful outcomes for the AUT community. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff. About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi , Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: 8–12+ years in IT, with at least 5 years in modern workplace, endpoint management, or digital workplace leadership, with demonstrable experience in: Leading and developing a high-performing team of technology specialists and leaders. Managing delivery priorities, investment planning, vendor relationships, and service performance. Fostering a culture of innovation, collaboration, continuous improvement, and digital curiosity. Ensuring modern, secure, scalable, and resilient digital workplace services. Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Systems, Business Information Systems, or a related discipline. A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: As agreed with the successful candidate Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $140 – 145k For further information : Contact Caroline Cranston, AUT Recruitment Consultant - caroline. cranston@aut.ac.nz Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 25 October 2026 at 5pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96740 Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week. At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96740 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 25 Oct 2026 17:00 Expertise IT Experience level (s) Management More details (document) PD 11040 - Technology Experience & Enablement Senior Manager.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 05 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=fAkbe": {
      "title": "Head of School/Dean of Business",
      "description": "Head of School/Dean of Business - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Head of School/Dean of Business Head of School/Dean of Business Lead one of New Zealand's largest and internationally recognised Businesss Schools. Shape the future of business education through innovation, interdisciplinary collaboration and real-world impact. Contribute to a newly merged faculty at a pivotal moment of opportunity and change. 5-year term as Head of School/Dean of Business (renewable by mutual agreement). Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works, AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT's Business School As one of New Zealand's largest and internationally recognised business schools, AUT Business School combines academic excellence with real-world impact. Supported by an engaged academic community and growing research capability, the School delivers innovative education, influential research and strong connections with industry, government and communities. With dual AACSB and EQUIS accreditation, and a culture of collaboration and continuous improvement, the School is well-positioned to further enhance its national and international reputation.With over 100 FTE academic staff and over $50M operating income, a portfolio of research entities and high levels of staff engagement, the School educates over 3,200 students (EFTS) and combines scale, reputation and impact with opportunities for further international growth. For more information on this role and AUT, please visit the online candidate guide HERE . The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi This is an exceptional opportunity to lead one of New Zealand's largest internationally accredited Business Schools at a pivotal point in its evolution. The role also offers the opportunity to help shape a newly merged faculty , building strong interdisciplinary connections while advancing the School's distinctive identity and ambitions. The incoming Head of School/Dean of Business will work with heads of department, research entity leaders and professional staff colleagues, building on strong foundations including dual AACSB and EQUIS accreditation. The role requires an experienced academic leader who can navigate an evolving higher education landscape and provide confident leadership in a large, complex and highly visible Business School. As a member of the Executive (Faculty) Dean's Leadership Team, you will provide strategic, academic and operational leadership of the Business School and contribute to overall faculty direction and decisions. Key focus areas include: Shape the future of the Business School, strengthening its reputation, impact and contribution across the University. Provide outstanding academic, operational and people leadership, leading colleagues while building a high-performing culture and developing future leaders. Drive excellence in teaching, research and engagement , advancing internationalisation and supporting Māori and Pacific success through AUT's Te Tiriti commitments and aspirations for Mātauranga Māori. Grow research quality, impact and external funding, translating knowledge into meaningful outcomes for industry, communities and society. Build strategic partnerships with industry, alumni, professional bodies, government and community stakeholders. Lead transformational change while fostering interdisciplinary collaboration and advancing AUT's strategic ambitions as a leading University of Technology. About you | Ko wai koe You'll bring an open, engaging and collaborative approach, with the flexibility to respond to changing requirements and actively contribute to a positive and collegial environment. You will demonstrate awareness and respect when engaging with culturally diverse communities. Experience supporting indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly desirable. Applicants should have the following characteristics: A respected academic leader, ideally at Professor level, with the credibility and strategic capability to lead a large and complex Business School. Significant people leadership and direct staff management experience, including leading large academic units or teams, developing others and fostering high-performing cultures. A strong track record in teaching, research and engagement, with a commitment to internationalisation, Māori and Pacific success and AUT's Te Tiriti commitments. Demonstrated success growing research quality, impact and external funding, including through interdisciplinary collaboration. Well-developed external engagement capabilities, with the ability to build strategic partnerships across industry, professional, government and community sectors. Proven strategic and change leadership experience, with the ability to navigate complexity and advance organisational priorities. Experience with AACSB and EQUIS accreditation processes is highly desirable. How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Please submit the following via AUT’s careers site: A cover letter detailing why this unique role and AUT appeal to you, and what impact and contribution you believe you could make. A statement addressing how your experience aligns with the key characteristics above. Your full CV (including a comprehensive publication list, research funding/grant acquisitions) and details of the scale, scope and impact of leadership roles held. Further Information: Start Date: Early-mid 2027 (to be agreed). Term: The successful candidate will secure a 5-year term, renewable by mutual agreement. Salary: NZD $180,000 - $245,000 per annum. Inclusive of a Head of School allowance and aligned with the appropriate step in AUT's academic pay scales (Professor or Associate Professor). For enquiries or a confidential conversation: Contact Mike Wood: AUT Executive Recruitment Partner – mike.wood@aut.ac.nz . Advertising closes: Sunday 1 November at 11.55pm NZST Timings: Shortlisting - Mid November; Interviews - Late November/early December. Reference: 96926. At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96926 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Fixed term Closes on 01 Nov 2026 23:55 Expertise Academic Management, Associate Professor, Executive, Management & Planning, Professor Experience level (s) Management, Executive More details (document) Candidate Information Guide https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/your-aut-candidate-guide-head-of-school-dean-of-business Posted on 05 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=j8kbe": {
      "title": "Executive Dean",
      "description": "Executive Dean - Faculty of Society and Business - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Executive Dean - Faculty of Society and Business Executive Dean - Faculty of Society and Business Shape the future of a bold new faculty , harnessing the strengths of diverse disciplines to create knowledge, research and partnerships that deliver real-world impact. Lead and inspire over 800 staff , fostering a high-performing culture that empowers outstanding teaching, research and student success. Influence at scale , shaping AUT’s interdisciplinary collaboration and strategic partnerships as a member of our Vice-Chancellor's Executive. 5-year fixed-term appointment based at AUT's City Campus in Auckland. Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works, AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Faculty of Society and Business AUT is merging its dynamic faculties of Business, Economics and Law and Culture and Society . The new faculty will educate over 6,100 students (EFTS) and offer an exceptional breadth of expertise uniting commercial, legal, social and cultural perspectives to address complex real-world challenges and create meaningful impact. Students will benefit from innovative, interdisciplinary learning that combines professional preparation with a deep understanding of people, communities and global trends. Academics will have exciting new opportunities for collaboration across diverse disciplines, driving research, partnerships and impact. With a strong focus on innovation, inclusion and future-focused thinking, this unique faculty will be a vibrant environment where students and staff can thrive, lead and make a lasting impact in Aotearoa and beyond. For more information on this role and AUT, please visit the online candidate guide HERE . The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We are seeking a visionary Executive Dean to provide outstanding strategic, academic and people leadership. You will help ensure the faculty's teaching, research and partnerships create real-world impact for students, industry and communities.  This is a rare opportunity to shape a distinctive faculty that brings together expertise across business, economics, law, social sciences, education, humanities and creative disciplines - creating powerful opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration, innovation and impact. You will lead and empower a faculty leadership team of eight direct reports, with overall responsibility for over 800 staff dedicated to transformational teaching, enhancing the student experience, and delivering high-quality, impactful research. We are ambitious, future-focused and open to adventurous approaches that challenge convention, embrace innovation and turn great ideas into reality. This role oversees an operating budget of circa NZD $118 million. As a member of the Vice-Chancellor's Executive, and a range of University governance and advisory bodies, you will play a pivotal role in shaping both the future of the faculty and the wider direction of AUT. Key focus areas include: Shape the future of a newly established faculty by successfully embedding the merger and realising the full potential of a bold, multidisciplinary vision spanning Business, Economics, Law, Culture and Society. Elevate research excellence, relevance and impact , driving stronger research performance, innovation, partnerships and reputation. Leverage the faculty's scale and diversity to drive interdisciplinary collaboration and greater academic, industry and societal impact. Strengthen and optimise the academic portfolio, enhancing programme quality, relevance and connectivity while creating seamless pathways for students across disciplines. Build a unified, high-performing culture, developing a strong shared identity, empowering staff and creating an environment where people, ideas and innovation thrive. Champion and advance the faculty's commitment to Te Tiriti o Waitangi, embedding AUT's Te Tiriti framework and strengthening Māori success, partnership and outcomes across all aspects of the faculty. About you | Ko wai koe You'll bring an open, engaging and collaborative approach, with the flexibility to respond to changing requirements and actively contribute to a positive and collegial environment. You will demonstrate awareness and respect when engaging with culturally diverse communities. Experience supporting indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly desirable. We welcome applications from ambitious and inspiring senior academic, business, industry and community leaders from both within and outside the university sector. Applicants should have the following characteristics: 1. An accomplished senior leader with expertise relevant to the faculty's disciplines, and a proven ability to deliver strategic, academic and organisational outcomes in complex environments. 2. Significant people leadership experience at scale , with proven capability to inspire, develop and align large and diverse teams, foster high-performing cultures and deliver results through others. 3. Suitability for appointment as Professor, either a record of academic achievement, research, innovation and professional impact or equivalent distinction through industry, professional practice or executive leadership. 4. A champion for equity, diversity and inclusion, with the ability to advance AUT's Te Tiriti commitments and strengthen Māori, Pacific and equitable outcomes. 5. Demonstrated success leading strategic change and transformation , bringing people together around a shared vision and embedding sustainable organisational change. 6. Proven success advancing research excellence, impact and innovation , building high-performing research environments and external partnerships. 7. Significant experience fostering interdisciplinary collaboration and innovation , leveraging diverse disciplines to strengthen research, education, partnerships and 8. Strong strategic, commercial and financial acumen, including experience building industry, community, international and stakeholder partnerships that deliver impact. How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Please submit the following via AUT’s careers site: A cover letter detailing why this unique role and AUT appeal to you, and what impact and contribution you believe you could make. A statement addressing how your experience aligns with the key characteristics above. Your full CV (including a comprehensive publication list, research funding/grant acquisitions) and details of the scale, scope and impact of leadership roles held. Further Information: Start date: Early-mid 2027 (to be agreed). Term: The successful candidate will secure a 5-year term, renewable by mutual agreement.  A competitive remuneration package will be agreed, commensurate with skills and experience. For enquiries or to arrange a confidential conversation: Contact Mike Wood: AUT Executive Recruitment Partner – mike.wood@aut.ac.nz . Advertising closes: Sunday 1 November at 11.55pm NZST Shortlisting: mid-November. Interviews: late-November/early-December. Reference: 96924. At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96924 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Fixed term Closes on 01 Nov 2026 23:55 Expertise Academic Management, Executive, Management & Planning, Professor Experience level (s) Management, Executive More details (document) Candidate Information Guide https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/your-aut-candidate-guide Posted on 05 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=mC0be": {
      "title": "Timetabler",
      "description": "Timetabler - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Timetabler Timetabler Central City-based role Great company and staff benefits Challenging and rewarding role directly benefiting staff and students Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT’s Estates Group is our award-winning in-house property and services team. Our mission: create inspiring, future-ready spaces that leave a lasting impact. The group manage the planning, development, operation, and maintenance of AUT’s property portfolio valued at $1.9 billion spread over 3 main campuses. From property services to commercial and hospitality operations, security and emergency management, we provide end-to-end solutions that underpin AUT’s mission to enrich lives through technology, learning, and discovery. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We are looking for a well-organised, flexible team member to help schedule timetables for students and staff.  Based at our City Campus, the successful applicant will work as part of our small team who are key to the operation of the University. You will need to be able to interpret requirements from staff, apply those to the software and be able to sanity-check the results. If you are well organised, can manage timelines and thrive in finding solutions to problems, this may be the role for you.  You will relate well to a variety of people and be able to manage conflicting requirements in a positive way.  There are plenty of opportunities to get out and interact with staff while also concentrating on and working through complex scheduling problems.  At the end of the day though, your efforts will have direct results for the staff and students of AUT. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi , Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: Proficient user of Excel Ability to find solutions to complex problems Ideally have a tertiary qualification and 3 years' practical experience in a relevant industry A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note: all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: January 2027 Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $76,000 - $102,000 per annum (dependent on experience and qualifications) For further information : please send us an enquiry or call 09 921 9499 Closing date | Te rā aukati: 19th October 2026, at 11:55 pm. Job reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96900 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96900 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 19 Oct 2026 23:55 Expertise Administration Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 1513 - Timetabler.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 05 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
