    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=nlxae": {
      "title": "Learning Specialist",
      "description": "Learning Specialist - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Learning Specialist Learning Specialist Design and deliver innovative learning experiences for diverse learners. Leverage emerging technologies and contemporary learning design practices to develop workshops, learning resources, AI and personalised one-to-one support Work with a passionate team of committed educational professionals 2-year fixed-term, full-time position based at AUT's City Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works, AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. About Te Mātāpuna Library & Learning Services Te Mātāpuna Library and Learning Services plays a central role in supporting student learning, academic success, and lifelong learning capability across AUT. Through expert learning support, information literacy development, digital capability building, and academic engagement initiatives, the team works collaboratively with students, faculties, and professional services to create an inclusive and empowering learning environment. As part of AUT's commitment to educational excellence and equity, Te Mātāpuna is on an ongoing indigenisation journey and contributes actively to AUT's commitment to Te Tiriti o Waitangi. The O pportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We are seeking an experienced and student-focused Learning Specialist to join our Learning and Academic Engagement team on a fixed-term basis. Reporting to the Senior Manager Learning and Academic Engagement, you will play a key role in developing and delivering inclusive academic learning support services that enhance the success of undergraduate and postgraduate coursework students. This role offers the opportunity to design and facilitate a range of learning interventions, including individual consultations, small-group sessions, workshops, orientation programmes, and learning resources. You will support students to strengthen their academic literacies, digital capabilities, study skills, and confidence in navigating university learning environments. Working closely with colleagues across Te Mātāpuna, faculties, and other university divisions, you will contribute to the design of innovative and accessible learning experiences. You will also monitor and evaluate programme effectiveness, using data and student feedback to continuously improve service delivery and student outcomes. This is an opportunity to make a meaningful impact on student success while helping shape academic learning support and development across the University and supporting AUT's Te Aronui journey. Please note this role will require some evening teaching. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you'll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff: https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you'll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff, and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We're looking for someone with energy, curiosity, and a passion for student success, who brings a collaborative and inclusive approach to their work. You'll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi, Indigenous peoples, and diverse communities. Experience supporting equity, accessibility, and inclusion-focused initiatives will be highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: experience with designing and delivering academic skills development and support strong relationship-building skills with the ability to collaborate effectively across a range of stakeholders experience using data and research to inform continuous improvement excellent written and verbal communication skills 5 - 7 years’ experience of relevant teaching in tertiary or secondary education a teaching qualification Master of Education, Master of Applied Linguistics or similar, or working towards a similar qualification Curiosity about and experience of working with AI and other emerging technologies for learning A commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion, and supporting AUT's Te Aronui journey How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which: a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest; and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT's careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: January 2027 Salary Range | Ngā Utu: $96,000 – $ 116,798 (dependent on experience and qualifications) For further information: please send us an enquiry or call 09 921 9499 Closing Date | Te rā aukati: Monday 26th October 2026, at 11: 55 pm. Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96852 Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week. At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96852 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Fixed term Closes on 26 Oct 2026 23:55 Expertise Accommodation, General & Administration, Administration, Campus Services, Exam Invigilator, Executive, Management & Planning, Finance & Estates, Health & Safety, Health Centre, Human Resources, IT, International, Library, Other, Public Relations, Registry Services, Security, Maintenance & Facilities Management, Student Services, Technician, Strategy, Students and Marketing Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 11064 - Learning Specialist.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 05 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
