    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=5LEbe": {
      "title": "Chief Executive",
      "description": "Chief Executive - AUT Ventures - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Chief Executive - AUT Ventures Chief Executive - AUT Ventures Lead one of New Zealand's most influential research commercialisation and innovation organisations. Turn bold ideas, research and innovation into meaningful impact. Drive the translation of world-class research into ventures, technologies and outcomes that create lasting value. Permanent, full-time position based in Auckland’s CBD. AUT Ventures AUT Ventures exists to turn bold ideas, research and innovation into impact. As AUT's commercialisation and consulting company, it connects world-leading research, entrepreneurial talent, investors and industry partners to create ventures, technologies and solutions that address real-world challenges. With a 20-year track record, a $5M Innovation Fund, and a growing portfolio of high-potential ventures and technologies, AUT Ventures plays a pivotal role in New Zealand's innovation ecosystem. From medical devices to sportstech, new materials to AI, creative technologies to seismic engineering and everything in between, AUT Ventures is helping shape industries, create economic, social and environmental value, and deliver meaningful outcomes on a global stage. To learn more about AUT Ventures, visit: https://ventures.aut.ac.nz/ For further details about the role, please review the position description. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi Lead the organisation responsible for transforming AUT's research, expertise and entrepreneurial talent into real-world impact. As Chief Executive, you will drive AUT Ventures’ strategic, commercial and operational success, leading a high-performing team of 12 specialists dedicated to creating pathways from discovery to impact through research commercialisation, venture development and consulting. This is a unique opportunity to be part of the future of innovation and research commercialisation in Aotearoa New Zealand, enabling ideas and discoveries to deliver social, economic and environmental benefits while strengthening AUT's contribution locally and globally. With a strong platform, established reputation and growing pipeline of innovation and commercialisation opportunities, AUT Ventures is well positioned for its next phase of growth and impact. This role offers a rare opportunity to shape the future of research commercialisation in Aotearoa New Zealand, working at the intersection of research, entrepreneurship, investment and industry to bring breakthrough ideas, technologies and research to the world.  The role reports to the AUT Ventures Board and works closely with AUT's Deputy Vice-Chancellor Research. Key focus areas include: Advancing the impact and commercialisation of AUT research , innovation and intellectual property. Leading and empowering a high-performing team across pipeline development, commercialisation, consulting services and industry engagement. Building enduring partnerships with researchers, industry, investors and the wider innovation ecosystem. Creating pathways from discovery to impact through venture development, licensing, knowledge transfer and investment attraction. Ensuring sustainable growth and long-term value creation for both AUT and AUT Ventures. Providing strategic leadership, governance and stewardship to support performance, compliance and responsible growth. About you | Ko wai koe We are seeking a strategic, empathetic senior leader passionate for innovation, entrepreneurship and unlocking the potential of research to create meaningful impact. You will bring the commercial expertise to realise opportunities, alongside values-led relationship-building skills to work effectively across academia, industry, government and investment communities. Most importantly, you are motivated by helping talented people turn ideas and discoveries into outcomes that benefit communities, the environment and the economy. To succeed in this role, you will bring: Proven executive leadership experience, with a track record of building high-performing, values-led teams and cultures. Significant experience in research commercialisation , intellectual property management , and translating innovation into tangible outcomes. Demonstrated success in venture creation, investment attraction and commercialisation , including licensing intellectual property, developing spin-out ventures and bringing new technologies to market. Strong relationship-building capability and credibility across New Zealand's research, industry, government, investor and innovation communities. Sound commercial, financial and operational acumen , with experience leading organisational performance, sustainability and growth. Exceptional communication , influencing and strategic stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to navigate complex environments and competing priorities. A relevant postgraduate qualification is desirable . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Please submit the following via AUT’s careers site: A cover letter detailing why this unique role and AUT appeal to you, and what impact and contribution you believe you could make. A statement addressing how your experience aligns with the key characteristics above. Your full CV (including details of the scale, scope and impact of leadership roles held). Furt her Information: Start Date: The successful candidate would join AUT by February 2027 (to be agreed). Term: The successful candidate will secure a permanent appointment. A competitive remuneration package will be agreed, commensurate with skills and experience. C ontact for enquiries or a confidential chat: Mike Wood, AUT Executive Recruitment Partner – mike.wood@aut.ac.nz . Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works, AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Closing date for applications: Sunday 8 November at 11.55pm NZST Reference: 96946 At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96946 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 08 Nov 2026 23:55 Expertise Executive, Management & Planning Experience level (s) Executive More details (document) Chief Executive - Job Description Oct 2026.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 13 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=s9cae": {
      "title": "Healthcare Assistant",
      "description": "Healthcare Assistant - Primary Care - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Healthcare Assistant - Primary Care Healthcare Assistant - Primary Care Interesting and varied role Work with multi-disciplinary professional services Full time (2 days City Campus, 2 days North Campus, 1 day South Campus) Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT’s award-winning Student Services and Administration directorate is dedicated to delivering exceptional student-centred experiences across the entire learner journey, from enrolment through to graduation and beyond. Bringing together high impact services in student administration, wellbeing and support, governance, systems, and operational delivery, the directorate works collaboratively with academic and professional teams to enable student success and institutional effectiveness. It offers professionals the opportunity to make a meaningful difference in a large, diverse university environment - combining purpose led work, continuous improvement, and a strong focus on equity, service excellence and positive outcomes for students and staff. To learn more about Student Support Services at AUT, please click here: https://www.aut.ac.nz/student-life/support-services The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We have an exciting opportunity to join our busy University-based Medical Centre.  This work is a combination of support in clinical practice and administration, both clinical and operational. Our AUT Medical Centre’s deliver primary care services offering integrated healthcare to students.  The successful applicant will have a warm personality with excellent communication and organisational skills.  You will be professional and proactive, and able to demonstrate care in triaging and supporting patients. With a commitment to providing first-class care services and a good command of written and spoken English, you will be well prepared to deliver to our diverse university population. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi , Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: 2 year’s experience as an HCA in Primary Care Highly organised with good attention to detail Experienced with Medtech Evolution an advantage Healthcare level 4 certificate an advantage A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $62,000 - $81,000 per annum (dependent on experience and qualifications) For further information : please send us an enquiry or call 09 921 9499 Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 27 October 2026, 11:55pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96809 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week This role is considered a children’s worker role and will be subject to safety checks as part of the Children’s Act 2014 . At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96809 Location (s) North Campus, City Campus, South Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 27 Oct 2026 23:55 Expertise Health Centre Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 9287 - Healthcare Assistant.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 13 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
