    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=YNmae": {
      "title": "Disability Administration Coordinator",
      "description": "Disability Administration Coordinator - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Disability Administration Coordinator Disability Administration Coordinator Lead the coordination of disability support resources that enable equitable access and success for AUT students Manage disability resource planning, timetabling and service delivery across AUT's campuses Play a key role in developing inclusive, student-centred services through collaboration and continuous improvement Permanent, full-time role based at AUT's City Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT’s award-winning Student Services and Administration directorate is dedicated to delivering exceptional student-centred experiences across the entire learner journey, from enrolment through to graduation and beyond. Bringing together high impact services in student administration, wellbeing and support, governance, systems, and operational delivery, the directorate works collaboratively with academic and professional teams to enable student success and institutional effectiveness. It offers professionals the opportunity to make a meaningful difference in a large, diverse university environment - combining purpose led work, continuous improvement, and a strong focus on equity, service excellence and positive outcomes for students and staff. To learn more about Student Support Services at AUT, please click here: https://www.aut.ac.nz/student-life/support-services The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi A new opportunity for a Disability Administration Coordinator in AUT’s Disability Support Service has become available on AUT’s City Campus.  The Disability Support Service plays a critical role in supporting disabled learners to achieve equitable access, participation, and success at AUT. As the Disability Administration Coordinator, you will play a critical role in ensuring students who are Deaf, neurodivergent, or living with a disability or medical condition receive timely and effective support throughout their studies. Reporting to the Disability Service Manager, you will coordinate resources, timetabling, and administrative processes to deliver a seamless, student-centred service. Working closely with students, faculty staff, and internal stakeholders, you will oversee the allocation of disability support resources, monitor service delivery, manage operational processes, and contribute to continuous improvement initiatives that enhance accessibility and student success across AUT. Key Responsibilities Coordinate the allocation of disability support resources to meet student needs and academic timetabling requirements. Manage resource planning and scheduling to ensure timely and consistent support services across AUT campuses. Approve and manage timesheets for all disability support resource staff; including the Disability Services Administrator, New Zealand Sign Language (NZSL) English Interpreters, digital note takers and academic assistants, ensuring accurate and timely processing. Monitor resource demand, identify trends and adjust resourcing to meet changing student requirements. Develop and maintain effective relationships with faculty staff, other key internal stakeholders. Lead continuous improvement initiatives to enhance service quality, operational efficiency and the student experience. Monitor service performance, maintain accurate reporting and contribute to operational and business planning. Ensure compliance with relevant legislation, university policies and quality assurance requirements. Support and develop a high-performing team through effective leadership and coaching. Leverage digital tools and systems to improve service delivery, reporting and operational effectiveness. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi , Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: Three or more years' team management experience A bachelor's degree or higher in a relevant field Expert-level administration and coordination experience, with the ability to manage workflows, resource scheduling, reporting and operational processes Experience coordinating resources, timesheet approval and service delivery within a busy, customer-focused environment Experience in tertiary education, community support or customer service A passion for supporting student success An ability to deliver high-quality, professional service with a culture of customer care Extensive experience with technology and relationship management software A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: Immediate start Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $76,000 - $102,000 per annum (dependent on experience and qualifications) For further information : please send us an enquiry or call 09 921 9499 Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 27 October 2026, 11:55pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96831 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96831 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 27 Oct 2026 23:55 Expertise Accommodation, General & Administration, Administration, Campus Services, Exam Invigilator, Executive, Management & Planning, Finance & Estates, Health & Safety, Health Centre, Human Resources, IT, International, Library, Other, Public Relations, Registry Services, Security, Maintenance & Facilities Management, Student Services, Technician, Strategy, Students and Marketing Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 11065 - Disability Administration Coordinator.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 13 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
