    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=y9Eae": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer - Paramedicine - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Lecturer - Paramedicine Lecturer - Paramedicine Bridging practice and education: Translate real‑world paramedicine experience into engaging, evidence‑based teaching that prepares students for the clinical, ethical, and decision‑making demands of pre‑hospital care. Developing future clinicians: Mentor and assess students across academic and simulation settings, supporting their progression toward safe, competent, and reflective professional practice. Contributing to the discipline: Engage in curriculum design, scholarship, and industry collaboration to ensure paramedicine education remains current, clinically relevant, and aligned with professional standards and workforce needs. Permanent, full-time, working at AUT’s South Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT's Paramedicine department is part of our School of Acute and Primary Health. The School is a leader in health education in Aotearoa New Zealand, delivering high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate programmes in oral health, paramedicine, midwifery and perioperative practice. These disciplines span the acute and primary care continuum, preparing graduates to work across diverse healthcare settings, from acute and emergency response, pre-operative, intra-operative and post-operative care to contributions in community-based and preventative healthcare services. The school’s unique combination of programmes reflects its commitment to integrated, person-centred healthcare that is responsive to both immediate and long-term needs. The School is part of our dynamic Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences . To learn more about our Health Sciences departments , please click here: https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/health-sciences The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We have a permanent, full‑time (37.5 hours per week) opportunity for a motivated Lecturer to make a significant impact and develop their career in teaching, research, and service. We’re open to expertise across areas relevant to our Paramedicine Department , and are particularly interested in applicants who can contribute to our teaching and research. We embrace practice-led, research-informed approaches to teaching for transformative student experiences that uplift communities. Your contributions to programme and course development will support our continuous-improvement focus. You will teach across programmes as assigned by the Head of Department and be comfortable using digital resources to enhance learning. You will publish actively in your specialised field/s. Research at AUT i s central to our mission, driving innovation, informing teaching and creating real-world impact for communities, industry and society. Over time, successful candidates are expected to seek and attract external research funding, engage with government, business, professional bodies and the community, and contribute to school/faculty activities. Please see the position description available for more information. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT, you’ll join a values-led university that supports you to thrive . We offer an excellent research environment with contestable research funds, and with guidance available from senior scholars. Benefit from flexible working, a supportive culture, cultural capability development for all staff, and strong growth opportunities – while advancing your impact through clear career pathways, recognition and research and teaching support. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . About you | Ko wai koe At AUT, academic staff combine teaching, research and engagement to create meaningful impact. You will work closely with students, collaborate across disciplines, and contribute to projects with industry, community and academic partners. We’re looking for academics with curiosity, energy and openness to new ideas , who are committed to collegiality, cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi, Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience contributing to Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. We welcome applications from Health Sciences academics. The selection criteria sought are: 1.Qualification: A Postgraduate qualification in Paramedicine or a related healthcare field is required Paramedicine registration is desirable but not mandatory not required, provided candidates bring relevant expertise applicable to paramedicine education 2.Research: An early career academic will have the basis of a solid research pipeline and a job market paper available. More experienced candidates will already have a more established research programme and a proven research track record with quality publications and ideally also success in external funding bids). Evidence of proactively pursuing external research income is desirable. 3.Teaching: An early career academic will ideally have at least some previous teaching assistant experience. More experienced candidates will have previous lecturing experience, evidence of curriculum development and preferably experience supervising Masters and/or PhD students. 4.Equity and Te Aronui Commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT's Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your full academic CV (including a complete list of publications, if applicable) please also submit: A cover letter which explains why this particular role (and AUT) is of interest and how your experience aligns with some, or all, of the selection criteria we're seeking above; A research plan outlining strategies to secure external funding, build research networks and establish collaborative partnerships (1 page max); Evidence of satisfactory student evaluations and innovation in teaching (2 pages max). A nominated journal or conference article All applications must be submitted through the online application process. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $94,000 - $112,000 per annum (appointment level and salary commensurate with skills and experience) For academic enquiries: Contact Bridget Dicker, Head of Department – Paramedicine, bridget.dicker@aut.ac.nz Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 10 November 2026, 11:55pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96861 This role is considered a children’s worker role and will be subject to safety checks as part of the Children’s Act 2014 . *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96862 Location (s) South Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 10 Nov 2026 23:55 Expertise Lecturer Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 1631 - Lecturer Paramedicine.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 13 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=VbQae": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer - Human Resource Management - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Senior Lecturer - Human Resource Management Senior Lecturer - Human Resource Management Shape the next generation of HR professionals through research-informed teaching Bring expertise in digital HR, people analytics and responsible use of technology Build strong links between research, industry and the evolving practice of HR Permanent, full-time academic opportunity based in Auckland Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works, AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT’s Department of Management, Technology and Organisation Researchers in AUT's Department of Management, Technology and Organisation have strong collaborative connections with employers, community organisations and policy makers. They enjoy the breadth of research, learning and teaching that the department offers, with multidisciplinary perspectives on people, work, organisations and technology. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We have a permanent, full-time (37.5 hours per week) opportunity for a motivated Senior Lecturer in Human Resource Management to make significant impact and develop their career in teaching, research and service. Digital technologies are rapidly shaping the way we recruit, develop, manage and support people at work. They also enable different ways to measure workforce and organisational culture. Within this change, the core foundations of good Human Resource Management, including ethical practice and an understanding of people and organisations remain essential. We are seeking a Senior Lecturer in Human Resource Management who’s research and teaching reflects cutting edge thought and practice. You will help develop and deliver engaging HRM learning experiences that connect established theory with the realities of contemporary workplaces. We are particularly interested in your expertise in digital HR and people analytics, including HR information systems, the interpretation of workforce data and the opportunities and challenges of AI in HR. Your teaching will encourage students to think critically, work confidently with evidence and make responsible, informed people-management decisions. Alongside teaching, you will advance your research and scholarship, publish high-quality work and build collaborations within and beyond the University. Connections with employers, professional bodies and communities will help keep both your teaching and research relevant to the HR profession. At Senior Lecturer level, you will also contribute to curriculum development, student supervision, mentoring and the wider academic life of the Department. Please see the position description available for more information. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT, you’ll join a values-led university that supports you to thrive . We offer an excellent research environment with contestable research funds , and with guidance available from senior scholars. Benefit from flexible working, a supportive culture, cultural capability development for all staff, and strong growth opportunities – while advancing your impact through clear career pathways, recognition and research and teaching support. A relocation package is available for those needing to relocate to Auckland. To learn more about our competitive staff benefits , please click HERE . About you | Ko wai koe As an academic member of staff at AUT, you’ll blend teaching, research and engagement to create outcomes that have real impact on the world. You’ll work closely with students, collaborate across disciplines and contribute to projects alongside industry and community partners.  With room to experiment, develop your skills and refine your practice, you’ll be supported to make a practical, impactful contribution to both learning and discovery. You will bring an open, engaging, and collaborative approach, with the flexibility to respond to changing requirements, and actively contribute to a positive and collegial environment. You will demonstrate cultural humility, awareness, and respect when engaging with indigenous peoples and culturally diverse communities. Experience supporting indigenous, equity, or inclusion focused initiatives is highly desirable. 1.Qualifications: A PhD in Human Resource Management, Employment Relations, HR Data Science or a closely related discipline. Strong expertise in HRM theory and practice, with specialist knowledge of digital HR, people analytics and the responsible application of HR technologies, workforce data and AI. 2.Teaching: Extensive university teaching experience, with demonstrated capability in curriculum development and delivering engaging, research-informed learning experiences. Experience supervising students, mentoring colleagues and contributing to academic development, alongside engagement with industry and the wider HR profession. 3.Research: An established research programme and proven track record of high-quality publications in peer-reviewed journals in HRM or related fields. Evidence of securing or contributing to external research funding, industry collaborations or research partnerships is desirable. 4.Equity and Te Aronui: A champion for equity, diversity and inclusion. Supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey ( https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/maori/auts-commitment-to-Te-Tiriti-o-Waitangi ). How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your full academic CV (including a publication list and details of research grants), please submit: A cover letter explaining your interest in the position and how your experience aligns with the requirements above. A research statement (one page maximum). Evidence of teaching quality and innovation (two pages maximum). All applications must be submitted through AUT’s online application process. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: 18/01/2027 Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $115,000 - $139,000 per annum (appointment level and salary commensurate with skills and experience) For academic enquiries: Contact Associate Professor Peter McGhee, Head of Department -Management, Technology and Organisation, peter.mcghee@aut.ac.nz Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 12 November 2026, 11:55pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96884 At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96884 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 12 Nov 2026 23:55 Expertise Lecturer, Senior Lecturer Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 11055 - Lecturer - Human Resource Management.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 13 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=5y1be": {
      "title": "Senior Manager",
      "description": "Senior Manager -  Built Assets - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Senior Manager -  Built Assets Senior Manager -  Built Assets Manage AUT’s high quality, sustainable Asset management environment Be a part of a team that provides a quality built environment for our students Permanent, full-time role based at AUT's City Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT’s Estates Group is our award-winning in-house property and services team. Our mission: create inspiring, future-ready spaces that leave a lasting impact. The group manage the planning, development, operation, and maintenance of AUT’s property portfolio valued at $1.9 billion spread over 3 main campuses. From property services to commercial and hospitality operations, security and emergency management we provide end-to-end solutions that underpin AUT’s mission to enrich lives through technology, learning, and discovery. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi This is a permanent, fulltime role that requires both clear strategic thinking and operational management skills.  The senior role is responsible for analysing data on over 25,000 key, technically complex assets and involves interaction with specialist external consultants and staff involved in the prioritisation, funding, planning, and execution of asset replacement or renewal projects. The successful applicant will be involved in projects from small refurbishments to new builds, so will have superb communication and facilitation skills, and will be able to encourage ongoing participation of internal and external stakeholders in the delivery of high quality and cost-effective asset management services. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff . About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi , Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: Significant (5+) years' experience in a similar role/ field Experience managing a large asset portfolio, ideally within an institutional environment and/or experience in the strategic development of a diverse asset portfolio. A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: January 2027 Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $120,000-$140,000 For further information : Contact Caroline Cranston, AUT Recruitment Consultant - caroline.cranston@aut.ac.nz Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 1/11/2026 at 5pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96903 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96903 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 01 Nov 2026 17:00 Expertise Finance & Estates Experience level (s) Management More details (document) PD 656 - Senior Manager - Built Assets.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 12 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=kIOae": {
      "title": "Kaiwhakaako (Lecturer)",
      "description": "Kaiwhakaako (Lecturer) - Core & Shared Courses - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Kaiwhakaako (Lecturer) - Core & Shared Courses Kaiwhakaako (Lecturer) - Core & Shared Courses Supporting curriculum delivery aligned with learning outcomes and assessment requirements Coordinating course delivery, Canvas sites, and student learning activities Monitoring student progress and supporting early intervention where needed Coordinating tutors and markers to ensure consistent and timely assessment Working collaboratively to ensure alignment and quality across programmes Permanent, full-time role based at AUT's North Campus in Auckland Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT’s Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences is a vibrant, interdisciplinary academic community committed to improving health, wellbeing and environmental sustainability locally and globally. The Faculty brings together leading educators, researchers and practitioners across health sciences, public health, rehabilitation, sport and exercise science, food science, chemistry, biology, biomedical science, and environmental science, with a strong emphasis on applied learning and real-world impact. Staff benefit from close links with industry, iwi, communities and government, opportunities for collaborative and translational research, and a culture that values innovation, equity and social responsibility. The Faculty offers an engaging, supportive environment for talented academics who want their teaching and research to make a meaningful difference in Aotearoa New Zealand and beyond. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We have a permanent, full-time (37.5 hours per week) opportunity for a motivated Lecturer to make significant impact and develop their career in teaching and service. We are open to expertise across areas relevant to our department , and are particularly interested in applicants who can contribute to our teaching and research in complementary topics such as (but not limited to: Teaching models Challenges faced by first-year health students (academic, emotional, social) Transition from school to university in health disciplines Development of academic literacy and study skills Innovative assessment Experiences of Māori, Pasifika, or other underrepresented students (relevant to NZ context) Culturally responsive teaching in health education Supporting students from diverse educational backgrounds We embrace practice-led, research-informed approaches to teaching for transformative student experiences that uplift communities. Your contributions to programme and course development will support our continuous-improvement focus. You will teach across programmes as assigned by the Head of Core Courses and be comfortable using digital resources to enhance learning. You will publish actively in your specialised field/s. Research at AUT is central to our mission, driving innovation, informing teaching and creating real-world impact for communities, industry and society. Over time, successful candidates are expected to seek and attract external research funding, engage with government, business, professional bodies and the community, and contribute to school/faculty activities. Please see the position description available for more information. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT, you’ll join a values-led university that supports you to thrive . We offer an excellent research environment with contestable research funds, and with guidance available from senior scholars. Benefit from flexible working, a supportive culture, cultural capability development for all staff, and strong growth opportunities – while advancing your impact through clear career pathways, recognition and research and teaching support. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . About you | Ko wai koe At AUT, academic staff combine teaching, research and engagement to create meaningful impact. You will work closely with students, collaborate across disciplines, and contribute to projects with industry, community and academic partners. We’re looking for academics with curiosity, energy and openness to new ideas , who are committed to collegiality, cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi, Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience contributing to Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. We welcome applications from Health and Social Science academics. The selection criteria sought are: Qualification: A Postgraduate qualification in a field relevant to their area of work. Research: An early career academic will have the basis of a solid research pipeline and a job market paper available. More experienced candidates will already have a more established research programme and a proven research track record with quality publications and ideally also success in external funding bids. Evidence of proactively pursuing external research income is desirable. (Lecturers) Evidence of securing or contributing to external research income is desirable. (Senior Lecturers) Teaching: An early career academic will ideally have at least some previous teaching assistant experience. More experienced candidates will have previous lecturing experience, evidence of curriculum development and preferably experience supervising Masters and/or PhD students. Equity and Te Aronui Commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT's Te Aronui journey All applications must be submitted through the online application process. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: To be agreed upon Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $94,000 - $112,000 per annum (appointment level and salary commensurate with skills and experience) For academic enquiries: Contact Nicola Power (Nicola.power@aut.ac.nz). Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 23rd November 2026, at 11:55 pm. Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96880 At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96880 Location (s) North Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 23 Nov 2026 23:55 Expertise Lecturer Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 10989 - Kaiwhakaako Lecturer CPL - Core Courses Coordinator.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 23 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
