    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=WDh4e": {
      "title": "International Senior Specialist",
      "description": "International Senior Specialist - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies International Senior Specialist International Senior Specialist Shape AUT’s global strategy and international growth. Partner with senior leaders to deliver international outcomes. Grow partnerships and enhance the international student experience. Permanent, full time role based on AUT's city campus. Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. The International Office plays a pivotal role in developing and strengthening the AUT's global presence, fostering international partnerships, Transnational Education (TNE), and ensuring the achievement of international student recruitment and engagement objectives. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We're looking for an experienced International Senior Specialist to join our International Office. This is a unique opportunity to partner with senior academic leaders to deliver faculty-level internationalisation strategies that enhance student recruitment, global partnerships, transnational education, student mobility and the international student experience. Reporting to the Director International, you will be the strategic connector between the International Office and the Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences . Working closely with the Dean, Deputy and Associate Deans, Heads of School and senior leaders, you'll provide trusted advice, identify opportunities for growth, and coordinate initiatives that strengthen AUT's international presence. These are highly collaborative roles requiring strong relationship management and the ability to influence across a complex, matrix environment. To be successful in these roles you will: Develop and deliver faculty internationalisation plans aligned with AUT's strategic priorities. Build trusted partnerships with faculty leadership and key stakeholders across the University. Identify and grow international partnership and Transnational Education (TNE) opportunities. Support international student recruitment, marketing, conversion and enrolment initiatives. Drive initiatives that enhance the international student experience, retention and success. Champion student mobility opportunities, including exchange, study tours and Collaborative Online International Learning (COIL). Use data and market insights to inform strategic decisions and measure success. Represent the International Office across faculty committees, projects and working groups. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for TeTiriti o Waitangi, Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: A relevant tertiary qualification. Significant experience in a strategic management or business partnering role, ideally within a university or international education environment. Experience developing and maintaining strategic partnerships. Knowledge of international student recruitment, international partnerships and/or Transnational Education (TNE). Outstanding communication, influencing and stakeholder engagement skills. A collaborative approach and the ability to work effectively across diverse cultural and professional environments. A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT's Te Aronui Journey. How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: To be agreed with the successful candidates Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $110,000 - $120,000 - commensurate with the skills and experience of the successful candidates. For further information : Contact Caroline Cranston, AUT Recruitment Consultant – caroline.cranston@aut.ac.nz Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 5 November 2026 at 5pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96225 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96255 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 05 Nov 2026 17:00 Expertise International Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 10999 - Senior Manager - Faculty International.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 22 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
