    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=JPXae": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Supply Chain Management",
      "description": "Lecturer in Supply Chain Management - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Lecturer in Supply Chain Management Lecturer in Supply Chain Management Bring expertise and/or an interest in digital transformation, sustainability or analytics within Supply Chain Management Guide students navigate contemporary supply chain challenges through engaging, research-informed teaching Develop your research, professional networks and academic career in a collaborative Business School Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works, AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT’s Department of Management, Technology and Organisation AUT’s Department of Management, Technology and Organisation (MTO) is part of our dynamic Business School, which holds EQUIS and AACSB accreditations. Our Supply Chain Management colleagues are committed to high-quality teaching, meaningful research and close connections and engagement with industry. The discipline brings together interests spanning digital transformation, supply chain sustainability and circular economy, supply chain optimisation, strategic procurement and buyer–supplier relationships. Through practical, research-informed learning and collaboration, we help students explore how supply chains can respond to changing business, technological and societal needs. To learn more about the Management, Technology and Organisation department, visit AUT’s department page. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi Supply chains shape how organisations operate, innovate and respond to change. At AUT, we are seeking a Lecturer in Supply Chain Management who can bring this evolving field to life for students. We particularly welcome expertise or interests in digital transformation, sustainability or analytics within supply chains. Working with colleagues across the department, you will design and deliver engaging learning experiences that connect core supply chain concepts with contemporary practice. You will contribute to curriculum development, support students from diverse backgrounds and explore effective ways to use digital resources and real-world examples to enrich teaching. You will also develop an active programme of research and/or scholarship, share your work through quality publications (if on a career path) and seek opportunities to collaborate with colleagues, industry and other partners. With access to a supportive academic environment and opportunities for professional growth, this role offers scope to build your academic profile while making a positive contribution to students and the wider supply chain profession. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT, you’ll join a values-led university that supports you to thrive . We offer an excellent research environment with contestable research funds , and with guidance available from senior scholars. Benefit from flexible working, a supportive culture, cultural capability development for all staff, and strong growth opportunities – while advancing your impact through clear career pathways, recognition and research and teaching support. To learn more about our competitive staff benefits , please click HERE . About you | Ko wai koe At AUT, academic staff combine teaching, research and engagement to create meaningful impact. You will work closely with students, collaborate across disciplines, and contribute to projects with industry, community and academic partners. We’re looking for academics with curiosity, energy and openness to new ideas , who are committed to collegiality, cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi, Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience contributing to Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. You will bring a sound foundation in Supply Chain Management, a genuine enthusiasm for teaching and a curiosity about the challenges facing organisations and supply chains. You will have a PhD in a related area, and you may already have university teaching experience or be developing your academic career, but you will share our commitment to making learning accessible, relevant and intellectually engaging. We value clear communicators and collaborative colleagues who are keen to contribute to a positive academic environment. You will be open to working across disciplines, building connections with professional practice and engaging respectfully with Māori, Pacific and diverse communities. The selection criteria sought are: Qualifications: A PhD in Supply Chain Management or a closely related discipline. Knowledge of contemporary supply chain theory and practice; expertise in digital transformation, sustainability and/or analytics in a supply chain context is highly desirable. Teaching: Experience in higher education teaching, tutoring or teaching assistance, with the ability to engage and support diverse learners. An interest in curriculum development and designing effective, research-informed learning experiences. The ability to relate supply chain concepts to contemporary organisational challenges and industry practice. Research: Evidence of a developing research agenda in Supply Chain Management or a related field, supported by research outputs or a clear publication pipeline. The potential to build research collaborations and pursue external funding opportunities is desirable. Equity and Te Aronui A champion for equity, diversity and inclusion. Supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your full academic CV (including a list of publications and any research funding), please submit: A cover letter outlining your interest in AUT and how your experience aligns with the selection criteria; A research statement (1 page maximum); Evidence of teaching effectiveness and innovation, such as student feedback or examples of teaching practice (2 pages maximum). All applications must be submitted through the online application process. Further Information: Start Date: April/May 2027 Salary Range: Career Path Lecturer - $96,000 - $115,000 per annum (appointment level and salary commensurate with skills and experience) Teaching Path - $88,000 - $104,000 per annum (appointment level and salary commensurate with skills and experience) Enquiries: Benjamin Dehe - Deputy Head of Department - Management, Technology & Organisation - benjamin.dehe@aut.ac.nz Closing date for applications: 19th November 2026, at 11:55 pm. Reference: 96896 At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96896 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 19 Nov 2026 23:55 Expertise Lecturer Experience level (s) Experienced (Less than 2 years), Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 715 - Lecturer and Senior Lecturer.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 20 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
